From: Ruhan <35257374+RuhanSA079@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radxa-cm3-io: enable CONFIG_AHCI_DWC for onboard SATA

The board's two SATA controllers (fc400000.sata / fc800000.sata,
enabled via the cm3-io-p1-sata/p2-sata devicetree overlays) advertise
compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-dwc-ahci", "snps,dwc-ahci". Only
CONFIG_SATA_AHCI_PLATFORM was enabled, which doesn't match either
compatible string, so the devicetree nodes came up with status=okay
but no driver ever bound to them (no /sys/.../driver symlink, no
ata_port). CONFIG_AHCI_DWC is the driver that actually claims this
DesignWare-AHCI variant.

---
 debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu b/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu
--- a/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu
+++ b/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu
@@ -2366,7 +2366,7 @@
 CONFIG_SATA_AHCI=y
 CONFIG_SATA_MOBILE_LPM_POLICY=0
 CONFIG_SATA_AHCI_PLATFORM=y
-# CONFIG_AHCI_DWC is not set
+CONFIG_AHCI_DWC=y
 # CONFIG_AHCI_CEVA is not set
 # CONFIG_AHCI_QORIQ is not set
 # CONFIG_SATA_INIC162X is not set
--
2.43.0
